  "step_3": "First, the information considered by the individual (expected value and probability of winning) does not align with the information required by the decision reason (aspiration level, differences from mean, probability of positive differences). The individual did not compute or refer to the aspiration level (2333.33 Euros) or the differences between outcomes and this level. Second, the justification provided (higher expected value and high 80% probability) does not match the rule of the decision reason, which prefers the lottery with higher probability of positive differences. In fact, the reason would prefer Lottery A (100% positive difference), but the individual chose Lottery B, which contradicts the reason’s preference. Therefore, the individual did not use the specified decision reason. The reasoning process described is based on expected value and probability magnitude, not on deviation from a mean-based aspiration level. There is no indication that the individual applied the rule of the decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
